.TH MEMTEST86 1 "August 2025" "memtest86 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
memtest86 \- memory diagnostic tool for deepin 25
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B memtest86
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B memtest86
is a memory testing utility inspired by memtest86, designed for deepin 25
systems. It runs various memory test algorithms to detect memory errors.
By default it starts the graphical (DTK6) interface; use
.B \-\-cli
for the command line mode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-cli
Run in command line mode (default is GUI).
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-size \fIsize\fR
Memory size to test, e.g. 256M, 1G, 512K (default: half of available memory).
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-passes \fIn\fR
Number of test passes (default: 1).
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-tests \fIlist\fR
Comma separated test ids, e.g. 0,2,4 (default: all).
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Verbose output.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help.
.SH TESTS
.TP
.B 0
Address test, walking ones
.TP
.B 1
Address test, own address
.TP
.B 2
Moving inversions, ones & zeros
.TP
.B 3
Moving inversions, 8-bit pattern
.TP
.B 4
Moving inversions, random pattern
.TP
.B 5
Block move, 64-bit moves
.TP
.B 6
Moving inversions, 32-bit blocks
.TP
.B 7
Random number sequence
.TP
.B 9
Bit fade test, 2 patterns
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
if the test passed (no memory errors detected),
.B 1
if errors were detected or the test failed to run,
.B 2
on invalid command line arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR memtest86 (8)
.SH AUTHOR
lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
